\section{The [[files edit]] subcommand}

[[files edit]] changes the two flags Canvas has for keeping a file from
students:
\begin{description}
\item[ [[--lock]] ] makes the file inaccessible to students; Canvas's file
  browser calls this \enquote{unpublished}.
  [[--unlock]] undoes it.
\item[ [[--hidden]] ] removes the file from the students' file browser but
  keeps it reachable through links, Canvas's \enquote{only available to
  students with link}.
  [[--visible]] undoes it.
\end{description}
The two are independent in Canvas, so they are two option pairs rather
than one state.
The selection is that of [[files list]], but the file regex is required
here, so that an edit never applies to every file of a course by default.
<<add files edit subcommand>>=
edit_parser = files_subp.add_parser("edit",
  help="Lock, unlock, hide or show files",
  description="Changes the locked and hidden flags of the selected files "
              "and prints them in the format of files list.")
edit_parser.set_defaults(func=files_edit_command)
add_file_options(edit_parser, required=True)
lock_group = edit_parser.add_mutually_exclusive_group()
lock_group.add_argument("--lock", dest="locked", action="store_const",
  const=True, help="Lock the files: students cannot access them")
lock_group.add_argument("--unlock", dest="locked", action="store_const",
  const=False, help="Unlock the files")
hidden_group = edit_parser.add_mutually_exclusive_group()
hidden_group.add_argument("--hidden", dest="hidden", action="store_const",
  const=True, help="Hide the files: only students with a link see them")
hidden_group.add_argument("--visible", dest="hidden", action="store_const",
  const=False, help="Show the files in the students' file browser")
@

An edit without a flag is an error before any request, since it would
only list the files.
Canvas answers an update with the updated file, which keeps the path and
course we computed for the old one: an edit does not move the file.
<<functions>>=
def files_edit_command(config, canvas, args):
  """Change the locked and hidden flags of the selected files."""
  changes = {key: value
             for key, value in [("locked", args.locked),
                                ("hidden", args.hidden)]
             if value is not None}
  if not changes:
    canvaslms.cli.err(1, "Nothing to change: give --lock, --unlock, "
                         "--hidden or --visible")
  output = csv.writer(sys.stdout, delimiter=args.delimiter)
  for file in process_file_option(canvas, args):
    try:
      updated = file.update(**changes)
    except Exception as e:
      canvaslms.cli.warn(f"Could not edit {file.path} in "
                         f"{file.course.course_code}: {e}")
      continue
    updated = canvaslms.cli.utils.ensure_file_attrs(updated)
    updated.course, updated.path = file.course, file.path
    output.writerow(file_row(updated))
@

Let's verify that only the given flags are sent, to every selected file,
and that an edit without flags stops before any request.
<<test functions>>=
@responses.activate
def test_edit_sends_only_the_given_flags(capsys):
  serve_listing(responses)
  for file_id, name in [(10, "lab1.pdf"), (11, "lab2.pdf")]:
    responses.put(f"{API}/files/{file_id}",
                  json=file_json(file_id, name, 2, locked=False, hidden=True))
  run(files_edit_command, canvasapi_course(Canvas(SERVER, "token")),
      file="^handouts/", folder=None, locked=None, hidden=True)
  updates = [dict(urllib.parse.parse_qsl(call.request.body))
             for call in responses.calls if call.request.method == "PUT"]
  assert updates == [{"hidden": "true"}, {"hidden": "true"}]
  rows = [line.split("\t") for line in capsys.readouterr().out.splitlines()]
  assert [row[1:5] for row in rows] == [
    ["handouts/lab1.pdf", "10", "unlocked", "hidden"],
    ["handouts/lab2.pdf", "11", "unlocked", "hidden"]]

def test_edit_without_flags_is_an_error():
  with responses.RequestsMock() as rsps:
    with pytest.raises(SystemExit):
      run(files_edit_command, canvasapi_course(Canvas(SERVER, "token")),
          file=".*", folder=None, locked=None, hidden=None)
    assert len(rsps.calls) == 0
